# Owner-visible alert for a failed control-plane check (VOYN-W0-AICC-
# CONTROL-PLANE-RESILIENCE). `%I` is the failing unit (systemd expands
# `OnFailure=aicc-control-plane-alert@%n.service` to the triggering unit's
# own name), fired by BOTH aicc-control-reconciler.service (control-01,
# escalated after its bounded retries are exhausted) and
# aicc-control-watchdog.service (worker-01, a heartbeat stayed stale past
# its SLO) -- one template, installed on both hosts, mirroring
# voyn-aicc-credential-rotation-alert@.service's existing pattern.
#
# A log line, not a paging integration: this repository has no owner contact
# channel to call out to. An operator (or a host-level log shipper watching
# `daemon.err`) is the audience -- wiring an actual page/notification is a
# host-specific follow-up, not something to fake here.

[Unit]
Description=Alert for a failed AICC control-plane check (%I)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/logger -p daemon.err -t aicc-control-plane "AICC control-plane check failed: %I -- a declared timer may be stopped, quarantined-but-still-active, or its tick's heartbeat stale past SLO; inspect 'journalctl -u %I' and the control_plane_event/control_plane_heartbeat tables immediately"
